/**
 * Evaluated data for heavy nuclides shown beside the liquid-drop model. These
 * are measured or evaluated values with their source; the model does not fit
 * them. Retrieved 2026-11-25. A field that could not be taken from an
 * evaluated source is null and is shown as "not available".
 *
 * halfLife, decay, bindingPerNucleon: IAEA LiveChart of Nuclides API
 *   (https://nds.iaea.org/relnsd/v1/data?fields=ground_states&nuclides=<A><symbol>):
 *   ENSDF adopted values (evaluation named per nuclide) and AME2020 masses.
 *   `systematics: true` marks a mass extrapolated in the evaluation.
 * beta2: from B(E2; 0+ -> 2+), NNDC adopted-entries file
 *   (https://www.nndc.bnl.gov/be2/data/adopted-entries.json): Raman, Nestor &
 *   Tikkanen, ADNDT 78 (2001) 1, and Pritychenko, Birch, Singh & Horoi,
 *   ADNDT 107 (2016) 1. Each entry is [value, uncertainty]. Even-even only.
 * barriers (MeV, inner and outer): IAEA RIPL-3 empirical-barriers.dat, entry
 *   of the nucleus itself. The IAEA host refused automated requests; the file
 *   was read from the Internet Archive capture of 2026-03-05.
 * d0: average s-wave spacing of target + n, RIPL-3 resonances0.dat (same capture).
 * resonances: ENDF/B-VIII.0 neutron sublibrary, MF=2 MT=151, l = 0 rows with
 *   positive energy inside the resolved range, ascending; energies in eV and
 *   neutron widths Γn in eV (first 100 at most). `count` is the number of such
 *   rows in the file. `statistics` is false where no single complete-looking
 *   sequence is available.
 * liquidDropBarrier (MeV): Cohen–Swiatecki interpolation with the
 *   Myers–Swiatecki surface energy; a model number, not a measurement.
 */
